A||||8||Johnny Bee||Reminiscing||||6||
Z||000000||Johnny Bee||09-28-2000||05:15 AM||||Hi all!  I just wanted to share a few fond memories of my high school days and my 1984 jet black Fiero.  <P>It was the Summer of '85.  Me, Guido, and Cockroach used to cruise around in "Black Beauty" with the driver's side window rolled down (the passenger's side often stuck) and Ted Nugent's "Wang Dang Sweet Poontang" crankin' on the radio.  I can't think of a better feeling than my foot pressing down on that gas pedal and the warm summer breeze coursing through my spiked hair.<P>I was 19 and about to begin my Junior year at Jefferson High in Piscataway.  I knew I would have to get a job before the first marking period began or I wouldn't be able to make the payments on "Black Beauty".  Luckily, my older sister worked at our local McDonald's restaurant and, through a bit of nepotism, I was working the drive-thru by August.  I saw a lot of Fiero's there!!!  <P>I can't believe how quickly time goes by!  A lot has changed since then.  Although I am still working the drive-thru, I had to get rid of "Black Beauty" two years ago.  She needed a new tranny and I just couldn't come up with the dough.  I came across a picture of the old girl while I was packing my stuff up last week to move from my parent's house into the room above their garage and it really brought back some memories!<P>Cheers!<P>------------------<BR>Fieros RULE!<p>[This message has been edited by Johnny Bee (edited 10-03-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||stimpy||09-28-2000||07:06 AM||||Now that's funny! It's always good to have a mullet-wearing hesher share their experiences. Say, who let you into the house to use the computer?<P>------------------<BR>Loud Pipes Save Lives!      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stimpy_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
