Z||000003||wkayl||09-29-2000||06:13 AM||||Yea, the good ol days.  My Jr year at Frederick, SDak high school (in 1972) I was working for my dad. We had a scrap iron business where I would go to auction sales and buy old farm machinery, cut it up with a torch, throw it on a flat-bed trailer or into our 1960 Studebaker 3/4 ton pickup and haul it into town.  But then again, my dad bought me my 1st car.  A 1953 Ford mainline 4 door.  now that was a chick magnet. "NOT"  He paid  $23.00 for it at a farm auction and $25.00 for another for parts to get it street ready.||||reg||1
